+In command mode, `v`, `V`, and `Ctrl-V` start character, line, and block visual selections in the
+focused pane. Visual mode uses `h`, `j`, `k`, `l`, and arrow keys to move the selection cursor, and
+`y` or `Y` emits `UiAction::CopySelection` with the selected text. `Y` in command mode copies the
+current focused-pane text line. Terminal adapters translate copy actions into one OSC52 clipboard
+sequence at the start of the next rendered frame.
